<main>
<!-- ================= HERO ================= -->
<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="overline">ISO 20022 Structured &amp; Hybrid Addresses &middot; November 2026 Deadline</div>
    <h1>Ten alternatives. Four categories.<br><span class="grad-text">One engine built for the structured-address mandate.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">We evaluated every serious alternative — postal platforms, LLM structurers, free network utilities, reference-data vendors and the in-house path — against the same 25-criterion framework for ISO 20022 structured and hybrid address compliance ahead of the November 2026 deadline. Here is the honest, normalized result.</p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href="#scoreboard">See the scoreboard
        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
      <a class="btn btn-outline btn-lg" href="#platform">Why a full application wins</a>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-band">
      <div class="kpi"><div class="kpi-value">4.90<span style="font-size:16px">/5</span></div><div class="kpi-label">Composite score &middot; 25 weighted criteria</div></div>
      <div class="kpi"><div class="kpi-value cyan">98%</div><div class="kpi-label">STP target on structured addresses</div></div>
      <div class="kpi"><div class="kpi-value teal">246</div><div class="kpi-label">Countries of postal reference data</div></div>
      <div class="kpi"><div class="kpi-value">2&ndash;4<span style="font-size:16px">wks</span></div><div class="kpi-label">Start in days &middot; live in weeks</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= CATEGORIES ================= -->
<section class="block" id="categories">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <div class="overline">The Landscape</div>
      <h2>Five ways teams try to solve structured addresses &mdash; and where each breaks</h2>
      <p>Every alternative below is a genuinely good product <em>for the job it was designed to do</em>. None of them was designed for SWIFT CBPR+ / SEPA payment-message compliance.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cat-grid">
      <div class="card card-accent cat-card reveal">
        <div class="head">
          <div class="icon-container ic-blue"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 10c0 6-8 12-8 12s-8-6-8-12a8 8 0 0 1 16 0Z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div>
          <div><h3>Postal Verification &amp; Geocoding Platforms</h3><div class="credit">Mature, certified &mdash; for mail delivery, not payment messages.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="chips"><span class="chip">Loqate (GBG)</span><span class="chip">Melissa</span><span class="chip">Smarty</span><span class="chip">AddressHub</span></div>
        <ul>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>A BIC or IBAN inside an address line is treated as unrecognised text &mdash; mislabeled, routed to &ldquo;Unmatched,&rdquo; or dropped.</li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>No SWIFT MT field parsing, no payment-chain party roles, no sanctions-screening connectors.</li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>Loqate&rsquo;s own docs warn a &ldquo;VerifiedLargeChange&rdquo; result may be <em>a completely different address</em> &mdash; a payment-misdirection risk without strict governance.</li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>Fitted to payments anyway: 26&ndash;40 weeks of custom build around the API.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-accent cat-card reveal">
        <div class="head">
          <div class="icon-container ic-cyan"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 8V4H8"/><rect width="16" height="12" x="4" y="8" rx="2"/><path d="M2 14h2M20 14h2M15 13v2M9 13v2"/></svg></div>
          <div><h3>AI / LLM Structurers</h3><div class="credit">Fluent converters &mdash; with stochastic cores or pilot-stage maturity.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="chips"><span class="chip">NTT Addresstune&trade;</span><span class="chip">StructX (Purple Fabric)</span><span class="chip">Catalyst DI</span></div>
        <ul>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>Generative AI in the critical path: non-deterministic output, EU AI Act exposure, no field-level rule citations a regulator can read.</li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>Structuring-only scope: no financial-ID ring-fencing, no historical name mapping, no de-duplication &mdash; a stack to assemble, not a drop-in.</li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>Little published evidence: no accuracy, latency or STP figures; APIs not publicly documented; ~18-week adoption incl. mandatory PoC.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-accent cat-card reveal">
        <div class="head">
          <div class="icon-container ic-teal"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2v20M2 12h20"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></div>
          <div><h3>Free Network Utilities</h3><div class="credit">SWIFT&rsquo;s own parser: a great first pass, by design a dead end.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="chips"><span class="chip">SWIFT AI Parser</span></div>
        <ul>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>Outputs 2 of 14 ISO 20022 address fields (Town + Country) as CSV/JSON &mdash; never compliant XML.</li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>No auth, no RBAC, no SLA, no health checks &mdash; 3&ndash;6 months of engineering to production-wrap.</li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>SWIFT&rsquo;s own guidance: transitional, planned end-of-life 2027&ndash;28 &mdash; a mandatory replacement project is built in.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-accent cat-card reveal">
        <div class="head">
          <div class="icon-container ic-blue"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><ellipse cx="12" cy="5" rx="9" ry="3"/><path d="M3 5v14a9 3 0 0 0 18 0V5"/><path d="M3 12a9 3 0 0 0 18 0"/></svg></div>
          <div><h3>Postal Reference Data Vendors</h3><div class="credit">Excellent data. Not a parser &mdash; and ioNova already embeds it.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="chips"><span class="chip">GeoPostCodes</span></div>
        <ul>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>Data tables, not a service: the entire parsing, correction, audit and integration engine remains to be built.</li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>ioNova ARS embeds this exact 246-country dataset &mdash; licensing ARS already includes it. &ldquo;Stacked, not substitutable.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-accent cat-card reveal" style="grid-column:1/-1">
        <div class="head">
          <div class="icon-container ic-cyan"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m18 16 4-4-4-4M6 8l-4 4 4 4M14.5 4l-5 16"/></svg></div>
          <div><h3>In-House Build</h3><div class="credit">Full control &mdash; and 18&ndash;36 months you don&rsquo;t have before November 2026.</div></div>
        </div>
        <ul style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:8px 24px">
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>246-country coverage, disambiguation, historical names and identifier ring-fencing built from scratch.</li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>A standing team to track EPC, PMPG, CBPR+ and per-country rule changes forever.</li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>Every month of build is a month closer to the deadline with nothing in production.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= SCOREBOARD ================= -->
<section class="block" id="scoreboard" style="background:var(--surface-1);border-block:1px solid var(--border)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <div class="overline">Normalized Scoreboard</div>
      <h2>All ten alternatives, one framework, <span class="grad-text">no asterisks</span></h2>
      <p>Every solution was scored on the same 25 weighted criteria (Signature Capabilities 48% &middot; Enterprise Operations 25% &middot; Payments Domain 15% &middot; Parsing Quality 12%), with risk penalties for zero-scores on signature capabilities and sub-2 scores on enterprise and payments criteria.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="table-wrap reveal">
      <table>
        <thead><tr>
          <th>Solution</th><th>Category</th>
          <th class="score-cell">Composite (0&ndash;5)</th>
          <th class="score-cell">Risk-adjusted</th>
          <th>Reqs met</th><th>Verdict</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="hero-row">
            <td>ioNova ARS</td><td>Purpose-built compliance engine</td>
            <td class="score-cell"><span class="score-num">4.90</span><div class="score-bar"><i class="brand" data-w="98"></i></div></td>
            <td class="score-cell"><span class="score-num">4.90</span><div class="score-bar"><i class="brand" data-w="98"></i></div></td>
            <td><span class="mono">25 / 25</span></td><td><span class="badge badge-green">Recommended</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="ionova-vs-catalyst-di-v5.html">Catalyst DI</a> <span style="font-weight:400;color:var(--text-muted)">(IntellectEU)</span></td><td>ML structurer &middot; GA Apr 2026</td>
            <td class="score-cell"><span class="score-num">2.72</span><div class="score-bar"><i class="mut" data-w="54"></i></div></td>
            <td class="score-cell"><span class="score-num">1.72</span><div class="score-bar"><i class="mut" data-w="34"></i></div></td>
            <td><span class="mono">20 / 25</span></td><td><span class="badge badge-amber">Pilot / component</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="ionova-vs-alpina-txflow-v5.html">Alpina TxFlow</a></td><td>Specialist MT&rarr;MX pipeline</td>
            <td class="score-cell"><span class="score-num">2.70</span><div class="score-bar"><i class="mut" data-w="54"></i></div></td>
            <td class="score-cell"><span class="score-num">1.20</span><div class="score-bar"><i class="mut" data-w="24"></i></div></td>
            <td><span class="mono">10 / 25</span></td><td><span class="badge badge-amber">Conditional &middot; EU sovereignty</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="ionova-vs-loqate-v5.html">Loqate</a> <span style="font-weight:400;color:var(--text-muted)">(GBG)</span></td><td>Postal verification platform</td>
            <td class="score-cell"><span class="score-num">2.22</span><div class="score-bar"><i class="mut" data-w="44"></i></div></td>
            <td class="score-cell"><span class="score-num">0.47</span><div class="score-bar"><i class="mut" data-w="9"></i></div></td>
            <td><span class="mono">13 / 25</span></td><td><span class="badge badge-amber">Postal layer only</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="ionova-vs-swift-ai-parser-v5.html">SWIFT AI Parser</a></td><td>Free open-source utility &middot; EOL 2027&ndash;28</td>
            <td class="score-cell"><span class="score-num">2.14</span><div class="score-bar"><i class="mut" data-w="43"></i></div></td>
            <td class="score-cell"><span class="score-num">0.00</span><div class="score-bar"><i class="mut" data-w="1"></i></div></td>
            <td><span class="mono">12 / 25</span></td><td><span class="badge badge-red">Free triage only</span></td>
